gredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Cornmeal  is a meal (coarse flour) ground from dried maize. It is a common staple food and is ground to coarse, medium, and fine consistencies, but it is not as fine as wheat flour can be. In Mexico and Louisiana, very finely ground cornmeal is referred to as corn flour. When fine cornmeal is made from maize that has been soaked in an alkaline solution, e.g., limewater (a process known as nixtamalization), it is called masa harina (or masa flour), which is used for making arepas, tamales, and tortillas. Boiled cornmeal is called polenta in Italy and is also a traditional dish and bread substitute in Romania."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-corn-meal"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corn_meal"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Southern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-southern-united-states",[["Chess pie","dish/chess-pie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Buttermilk","ingredient/buttermilk"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Granulated sugar","ingredient/granulated-sugar"],["Shortcrust pastry","ingredient/shortcrust-pastry"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1d/Polenta_uncooked.jpg/500px-Polenta_uncooked.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Popo le Chien","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polenta_uncooked.jpg"}},"ingredient/tylorrhynchus-heterochetus":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/tylorrhynchus-heterochetus","n":"Tylorrhynchus heterochetus","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Tylorrhynchus heterochetus, also known as the Japanese palolo is a species of edible ragworm."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"i